# Wrong output (PLAN.md): `%v.x` is a register of its own, apart from the
# vector register %v, so after a load overwrites %v it is still the
# thread index: the store's address reads 4 * %tid.x + param_0, 4 to 5
# sectors per warp request. ptxas takes the address from the load. The
# `.reg .v2` declaration the parser does not read is no instruction, so
# the first block's annotation is on its first instruction.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/vector_register.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}	ld.param.u64 	%rd1, [micro_vector_register_param_0]; // [<block 0>] warp * × lane * | exec 32/CTA{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store [4·%tid.x + param_0] sectors/req 4–5 (ideal 4){{$}}
